"</Accordion>\n"
"This page shows how to use the [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) class. For a high-level overview of operator representations in Qiskit, including the `Operator` class and others, see [Overview of operator classes](/guides/operators-overview).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Halaman ini menunjukkan cara menggunakan kelas [`Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator). Untuk gambaran keseluruhan peringkat tinggi tentang perwakilan operator dalam Qiskit, termasuk kelas `Operator` dan lain-lain, lihat [Gambaran keseluruhan kelas operator](/guides/operators-overview).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convert classes to Operators {#convert-classes-to-operators}"
msgstr "Tukar kelas kepada Operator {#convert-classes-to-operators}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Several other classes in Qiskit can be directly converted to an `Operator` object using the operator initialization method. For example:\n"
msgstr "Beberapa kelas lain dalam Qiskit boleh ditukar secara langsung kepada objek `Operator` menggunakan kaedah permulaan operator. Contohnya:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Pauli` objects\n"
msgstr "Objek `Pauli`\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Gate` and `Instruction` objects\n"
msgstr "Objek `Gate` dan `Instruction`\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`QuantumCircuit` objects\n"
msgstr "Objek `QuantumCircuit`\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the last point means you can use the `Operator` class as a unitary simulator to compute the final unitary matrix for a quantum circuit, without having to call a simulator backend. If the circuit contains any unsupported operations, an exception is raised. Unsupported operations are: measure, reset, conditional operations, or a gate that does not have a matrix definition or decomposition in terms of gate with matrix definitions.\n"
msgstr "Ambil perhatian bahawa perkara terakhir bermakna anda boleh menggunakan kelas `Operator` sebagai simulator kesatuan untuk mengira matriks kesatuan akhir bagi Circuit kuantum, tanpa perlu memanggil Backend simulator. Jika Circuit mengandungi sebarang operasi yang tidak disokong, pengecualian akan dilemparkan. Operasi yang tidak disokong ialah: ukur, tetapkan semula, operasi bersyarat, atau gate yang tidak mempunyai definisi matriks atau penguraian dari segi gate dengan definisi matriks.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use Operators in circuits {#use-operators-in-circuits}"
msgstr "Gunakan Operator dalam Circuit {#use-operators-in-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unitary `Operators` can be directly inserted into a `QuantumCircuit` using the `QuantumCircuit.append` method. This converts the `Operator` into a `UnitaryGate` object, which is added to the circuit.\n"
msgstr "`Operators` unitari boleh dimasukkan terus ke dalam `QuantumCircuit` menggunakan kaedah `QuantumCircuit.append`. Ini menukar `Operator` kepada objek `UnitaryGate`, yang ditambah ke dalam Circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the operator is not unitary, an exception is raised. This can be checked using the `Operator.is_unitary()` function, which returns `True` if the operator is unitary and `False` otherwise.\n"
msgstr "Jika operator bukan kesatuan, pengecualian akan dilemparkan. Ini boleh diperiksa menggunakan fungsi `Operator.is_unitary()`, yang mengembalikan `True` jika operator adalah kesatuan dan `False` sebaliknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/operator-class/extracted-outputs/223c07c9-1b1d-4a33-a397-091cac2ec9e3-0.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/operator-class/extracted-outputs/223c07c9-1b1d-4a33-a397-091cac2ec9e3-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that in the above example the operator is initialized from a `Pauli` object. However, the `Pauli` object may also be directly inserted into the circuit itself and will be converted into a sequence of single-qubit Pauli gates:\n"
msgstr "Ambil perhatian bahawa dalam contoh di atas operator dimulakan dari objek `Pauli`. Walau bagaimanapun, objek `Pauli` juga boleh dimasukkan secara langsung ke dalam Circuit itu sendiri dan akan ditukar kepada urutan gate Pauli satu qubit:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combine Operators {#combine-operators}"
msgstr "Gabungkan Operator {#combine-operators}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operators may be combined using several methods.\n"
msgstr "Operator boleh digabungkan menggunakan beberapa kaedah.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tensor product {#tensor-product}"
msgstr "Hasil darab tensor {#tensor-product}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two operators $A$ and $B$ can be combined into a tensor product operator $A\\otimes B$ using the `Operator.tensor` function. Note that if both $A$ and $B$ are single-qubit operators, then `A.tensor(B)` = $A\\otimes B$ will have the subsystems indexed as matrix $B$  on subsystem 0, and matrix $A$ on subsystem 1.\n"
msgstr "Dua operator $A$ dan $B$ boleh digabungkan menjadi operator hasil darab tensor $A\\otimes B$ menggunakan fungsi `Operator.tensor`. Ambil perhatian bahawa jika kedua-dua $A$ dan $B$ adalah operator satu qubit, maka `A.tensor(B)` = $A\\otimes B$ akan mempunyai subsistem yang diindeks sebagai matriks $B$ pada subsistem 0, dan matriks $A$ pada subsistem 1.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tensor expansion {#tensor-expansion}"
msgstr "Pengembangan tensor {#tensor-expansion}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A closely related operation is `Operator.expand`, which acts like a tensor product but in the reverse order. Hence, for two operators $A$ and $B$ you have `A.expand(B)` = $B\\otimes A$ where the subsystems are indexed as matrix $A$ on subsystem 0, and matrix $B$ on subsystem 1.\n"
msgstr "Operasi yang berkaitan rapat ialah `Operator.expand`, yang bertindak seperti hasil darab tensor tetapi dalam urutan terbalik. Oleh itu, untuk dua operator $A$ dan $B$ anda mempunyai `A.expand(B)` = $B\\otimes A$ di mana subsistem diindeks sebagai matriks $A$ pada subsistem 0, dan matriks $B$ pada subsistem 1.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Composition {#composition}"
msgstr "Komposisi {#composition}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also compose two operators $A$ and $B$ to implement matrix multiplication using the `Operator.compose` method. `A.compose(B)` returns the operator with matrix $B.A$:\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh mengarang dua operator $A$ dan $B$ untuk melaksanakan pendaraban matriks menggunakan kaedah `Operator.compose`. `A.compose(B)` mengembalikan operator dengan matriks $B.A$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also compose in the reverse order by applying $B$ in front of $A$ using the `front` kwarg of `compose`:  `A.compose(B, front=True)` = $A.B$:\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh mengarang dalam urutan terbalik dengan menerapkan $B$ di hadapan $A$ menggunakan argumen `front` dari `compose`: `A.compose(B, front=True)` = $A.B$:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subsystem composition {#subsystem-composition}"
msgstr "Komposisi subsistem {#subsystem-composition}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the previous compose requires that the total output dimension of the first operator $A$ is equal to the total input dimension of the composed operator $B$ (and similarly, the output dimension of $B$ must be equal to the input dimension of $A$ when composing with `front=True`).\n"
msgstr "Ambil perhatian bahawa komposisi sebelumnya memerlukan dimensi output keseluruhan operator pertama $A$ adalah sama dengan dimensi input keseluruhan operator yang dikarang $B$ (dan begitu juga, dimensi output $B$ mesti sama dengan dimensi input $A$ apabila mengarang dengan `front=True`).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also compose a smaller operator with a selection of subsystems on a larger operator using the `qargs` kwarg of `compose`, either with or without `front=True`. In this case, the relevant input and output dimensions of the subsystems being composed must match. *Note that the smaller operator must always be the argument of the* `compose` *method.*\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh mengarang operator yang lebih kecil dengan pilihan subsistem pada operator yang lebih besar menggunakan argumen `qargs` dari `compose`, sama ada dengan atau tanpa `front=True`. Dalam kes ini, dimensi input dan output yang relevan bagi subsistem yang dikarang mesti sepadan. *Ambil perhatian bahawa operator yang lebih kecil mesti sentiasa menjadi argumen kaedah* `compose`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, to compose a two-qubit gate with a three-qubit operator:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, untuk mengarang gate dua qubit dengan operator tiga qubit:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Linear combinations {#linear-combinations}"
msgstr "Gabungan linear {#linear-combinations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operators may also be combined using standard linear operators for addition, subtraction, and scalar multiplication by complex numbers.\n"
msgstr "Operator juga boleh digabungkan menggunakan operator linear standard untuk penambahan, penolakan, dan pendaraban skalar dengan nombor kompleks.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An important point is that while `tensor`, `expand`, and `compose` preserves the unitarity of unitary operators, linear combinations do not; hence, adding two unitary operators will, in general, result in a non-unitary operator:\n"
msgstr "Perkara penting ialah walaupun `tensor`, `expand`, dan `compose` memelihara kesatuan operator kesatuan, gabungan linear tidak; oleh itu, menambah dua operator kesatuan akan, secara umum, menghasilkan operator bukan kesatuan:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implicit conversion to Operators {#implicit-conversion-to-operators}"
msgstr "Penukaran tersirat kepada Operator {#implicit-conversion-to-operators}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that for all the following methods, if the second object is not already an `Operator` object, it is implicitly converted into one by the method. This means that matrices can be passed in directly without being explicitly converted to an `Operator` first. If the conversion is not possible, an exception is raised.\n"
msgstr "Ambil perhatian bahawa untuk semua kaedah berikut, jika objek kedua belum pun merupakan objek `Operator`, ia akan ditukar secara tersirat kepada satu oleh kaedah itu. Ini bermakna matriks boleh dihantar secara langsung tanpa ditukar secara eksplisit kepada `Operator` terlebih dahulu. Jika penukaran tidak mungkin, pengecualian akan dilemparkan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare Operators {#compare-operators}"
msgstr "Bandingkan Operator {#compare-operators}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operators implement an equality method that can be used to check if two operators are approximately equal.\n"
msgstr "Operator melaksanakan kaedah kesamaan yang boleh digunakan untuk memeriksa sama ada dua operator adalah lebih kurang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that this checks that each matrix element of the operators is approximately equal; two unitaries that differ by a global phase are not considered equal:\n"
msgstr "Ambil perhatian bahawa ini memeriksa bahawa setiap elemen matriks operator adalah lebih kurang sama; dua kesatuan yang berbeza dengan fasa global tidak dianggap sama:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Process fidelity {#process-fidelity}"
msgstr "Kesetiaan proses {#process-fidelity}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also compare operators using the `process_fidelity` function from the *Quantum Information* module. This is an information-theoretic quantity for how close two quantum channels are to each other, and in the case of unitary operators it does not depend on global phase.\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh membandingkan operator menggunakan fungsi `process_fidelity` dari modul *Maklumat Kuantum*. Ini adalah kuantiti teori maklumat untuk seberapa dekat dua saluran kuantum antara satu sama lain, dan dalam kes operator kesatuan ia tidak bergantung pada fasa global.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that process fidelity is generally only a valid measure of closeness if the input operators are unitary (or CP in the case of quantum channels), and an exception is raised if the inputs are not CP.\n"
msgstr "Ambil perhatian bahawa kesetiaan proses umumnya hanya merupakan ukuran kedekatan yang sah jika operator input adalah kesatuan (atau CP dalam kes saluran kuantum), dan pengecualian dilemparkan jika input bukan CP.\n"

